# Phone layout: Workspaces, Projects, Reviewers, Settings, Login, drawers, dialogs, toasts

## What to build

Make the rest of the graph-manager web UI fit a phone (360–430 px wide) with no sideways page scroll: at a 390 × 844 viewport, `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth` on `/workspaces`, `/projects`, `/reviewers`, `/settings` and the login page, and every drawer (Clone, Workspace settings, Reviewer; the shared `ui/Drawer.tsx`) and dialog (`ui/Dialog.tsx` `ConfirmDialog`, `ProjectDialog`) fits the screen with its header and buttons reachable. The work is CSS in `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/{Workspaces,Projects,Reviewers,Settings,Login}.css` and in the Drawer / Dialog / Toast section of `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/base.css` (lines 182–228), plus a structure test for Drawer and Dialog. Below 600 px the Workspaces, Projects and Reviewers rows become cards whose action buttons wrap onto their own line, filters are full width, the Clone forge choice is one column, `.sandbox-fields` is one column, `.settings-appearance-text` has `min-width: 0`, and the Login card padding is `--space-5`. Drawers keep their header and footer on screen and scroll only their body within `var(--app-h)`; dialogs are at most the screen width minus 32 px and `calc(var(--app-h, 100dvh) - 32px)` tall with a scrolling body; toasts sit above the home-bar safe area. Desktop (900 px and wider) must look exactly as today.

Already delivered by a dependency (in the codebase now; do not re-implement):
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/media.ts` exports `NARROW = "(max-width: 899.98px)"`, `PHONE = "(max-width: 599.98px)"`, `COARSE = "(pointer: coarse)"` and `useMedia(query): boolean` (it returns `false` when `window.matchMedia` is missing, as in jsdom).
- `--app-h` is set on `<html>` to the visual viewport height in px (it shrinks when the phone keyboard opens on iOS). Use `var(--app-h, 100dvh)` for every height.
- `ui/base.css` has `@media (pointer: coarse)` rules: 40 px hit areas on shared buttons (`.btn`, icon buttons, segmented options, list rows) and `font-size: 16px` on `input`, `select`, `textarea`.
- Safe-area padding (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`) on `.gm-shell`, toasts (`.toast-stack`), `.drawer-footer` and the dialog actions. Read `ui/base.css` first: keep those rules, do not add a second copy, and build on them.

In CSS, write the breakpoints as literal media queries: `@media (max-width: 599.98px)` (PHONE) and `@media (max-width: 899.98px)` (NARROW). Existing blocks at `max-width: 900px` / `480px` stay unless a step says to change them.

Out of scope (other tasks edit these files in parallel; do not touch them): `Shell.tsx`/`Shell.css`, `CommandPalette.tsx`, the Terminals page (`Terminals.*`, `TerminalPane.tsx`, its `.new-term-dialog`), the run pages (`Runs.*`, `RunDetail.*`, `PrPanel.*`, `TaskGraph.*`, `PhaseCards.tsx`, `StartRunDrawer.tsx`, `RunOptionsFields.tsx`) and `packages/graph-execution`. A later task adds an "Install app" section to `Settings.tsx`: keep Settings changes CSS-only (`Settings.css`); do not restructure `Settings.tsx`.

## Context: files to read before implementing

