## Patterns to follow

**CSS conventions:** tokens only, compact one-line rules like the existing files, a short comment above each block. Put each phone block after the rules it overrides (end of the file, or after the 900 px block), so it wins at equal specificity. The existing card pattern to extend (`Workspaces.css:99-117`):

```css
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .ws-table .ws-row.table-row {
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto; grid-template-areas: "forge repo tree" "branch runs actions"; row-gap: 6px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
  }
  .ws-forge { grid-area: forge; }
  ...
}
```

**Drawer layout:** header and footer are fixed-size flex children, only `.drawer-body` scrolls (`flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow: auto`, already in base.css line 192). The phone fix is the drawer's height, so iOS (whose layout viewport does not shrink for the keyboard) keeps the footer above the keyboard: `height: var(--app-h, 100dvh)` instead of `bottom: 0`.

**Test pattern:** jsdom computes no layout, so test structure the CSS relies on, mirroring `ui/components.test.tsx:57-100`:

```tsx
render(<Drawer open title="T" onClose={() => {}} footer={<button>Save</button>} testId="d"><p>body</p></Drawer>);
const d = screen.getByTestId("d");
expect([...d.children].map((c) => c.className)).toEqual(["drawer-header", "drawer-body", "drawer-footer"]);
```

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/base.css` (Drawer, Dialog, Toasts: lines 182–228 only)

- **IMPLEMENT** Drawer, after line 194:
  ```css
  /* The drawer is as tall as the visual viewport (iOS keyboard), so its header and footer stay on screen. */
  .drawer { bottom: auto; height: var(--app-h, 100dvh); }
  .drawer-header, .drawer-footer { flex: none; }
  .drawer-body { overscroll-behavior: contain; }
  .drawer-footer { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .drawer-header { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-4) 0; }
    .drawer-body { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .drawer-footer { padding-left: var(--space-4); padding-right: var(--space-4); }
  }
  ```
  Keep the dependency's `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` padding on `.drawer-footer` (if it set `padding-bottom`, do not override `padding-bottom` here). Keep `@media (max-width: 900px) { .drawer { width: 100%; } }`. On a drawer with no footer (Clone), the last result must clear the home bar: the dependency already adds `.drawer-body:last-child { padding-bottom: calc(var(--space-5) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) }` and `.drawer { padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top) }`; check they are there and add them only if missing (never twice).
- **IMPLEMENT** Dialog, after line 211:
  ```css
  /* A dialog never overflows the screen: 16px margin each side (the overlay padding), scrolls when too tall. */
  .dialog-overlay { padding: max(var(--space-4), env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px)) max(var(--space-4), env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px)) max(var(--space-4), env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)) max(var(--space-4), env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px)); height: var(--app-h, 100dvh); bottom: auto; }
  .dialog { max-height: calc(var(--app-h, 100dvh) - 32px); overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; }
  .dialog-title, .dialog-actions { flex: none; }
  .dialog-body { flex: 0 1 auto; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .dialog { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .dialog-actions .btn { flex: 1 1 auto; }
  }
  ```
  The required width is `calc(100% - 32px)` of the screen: the overlay's 16 px padding on each side already gives that with `width: 100%`, so do not subtract 32 px again inside the padded overlay (that would leave 64 px). Keep `.dialog { width: 100%; max-width: 420px; }` (line 205): at a 360 px viewport the dialog is then 328 px wide. `.dialog-body` shrinks first, so a `ConfirmDialog` with a long body keeps its title and buttons visible and scrolls the body; a dialog without `.dialog-body` (ProjectDialog, the Terminals new-terminal dialog) scrolls as a whole via `.dialog { overflow-y: auto }`.
- **IMPLEMENT** Toasts, after line 228:
  ```css
  /* Phone: toasts span the width and clear the home bar. */
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .toast-stack { left: var(--space-3); right: var(--space-3); width: auto; }
  }
  ```
  Check that `.toast-stack` `bottom` already includes `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` (dependency). If not, set `bottom: calc(var(--space-4) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));` on `.toast-stack`. Do not add anything about the terminal extra-keys row (the Terminals task owns that).
- **IMPLEMENT** touch: keyboard hints are useless on a touch screen and make footers wrap: `@media (pointer: coarse) { .drawer-footer .kbd, .dialog-actions .kbd { display: none; } }`.
- **GOTCHA**: do not edit the rest of base.css (the dependency's coarse/safe-area rules, `.btn`, `.input`, tables): other tasks build on them.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run lint`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Workspaces.css`

- **IMPLEMENT**: at the end:
  ```css
  /* Phone: cards with the actions on their own line, full-width filter, one-column forge choice. */
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .ws-header .ws-filter { flex: 1 1 100%; order: 2; }
    .ws-header .btn-primary { order: 3; flex: 1 1 100%; justify-content: center; }
    .ws-table .ws-row.table-row {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      grid-template-areas: "forge repo tree" "branch branch runs" "actions actions actions";
    }
    .ws-actions { flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-start; }
    .ws-actions > .btn { flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 6px); justify-content: center; }
    .ws-delete-wrap { flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .ws-note { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
