  `.login-card .input` (line 13) sets `font: 14px/1.4 …`. The dependency's coarse rule in base.css sets `font-size: 16px !important` on text inputs, which wins; confirm it is there. Only if it is not `!important`, add `@media (pointer: coarse) { .login-card .input { font-size: 16px; } }` here, or iOS zooms on the password field. The login page is rendered by `App.tsx:63` outside the Shell, so the Shell's safe-area padding does not apply: hence the `env()` here.
